    "title": "First United Methodist Church of Leechburg observes Good Friday with its annual outdoor service",
    "text": "The Rev. James Arter of the First United Methodist Church of Leechburg pulls a wagon containing wooden crosses as he begins the church’s annual Good Friday Crosswalk, symbolizing Jesus carrying the cross, while participants follow on Friday, April 3, 2026. (Massoud Hossaini | TribLive) The Rev. James Arter of the First United Methodist Church of Leechburg and participants of the church’s annual Good Friday Crosswalk stop for a Bible reading in the street on Good Friday, April 3, 2026. (Massoud Hossaini | TribLive) Mason Graham, 6, and his sister, Skylar, 4, both of Natrona Heights, assist the Rev. James Arter of the First United Methodist Church of Leechburg in installing a cross on a Leechburg street as the church begins its annual Good Friday crosswalk on Friday, April 3, 2026. (Massoud Hossaini | TribLive) The Rev. James Arter of First United Methodist Church of Leechburg pulls a wagon full of wooden crosses as he begins the church’s annual Good Friday Crosswalk, symbolizing Jesus carrying the cross, while participants follow on Friday, April 3, 2026. (Massoud Hossaini | TribLive) The Rev. James Arter (third from left) speaks in front of the First United Methodist Church in Leechburg as he begins the church’s annual Good Friday Crosswalk on Friday. (Massoud Hossaini | TribLive)",
